      'CHAPTER 4: THE GREAT BENEFICS & THE KARMIC AUDITOR\n\n5. BRIHASPATI (JUPITER) — Wisdom, Dharma, and Divine Grace\n• Sanskrit Names: Guru, Deva-Guru, Jeeva, Angirasa\n• Nature: Supreme Natural Benefic (Sattva), Ether/Akasha element, Brahmin teacher\n• Governance: Children (Santana), husband in female charts, higher philosophy, banking, law, dharma, liver, adipose tissue, spiritual mentors.\n• Dignities: Exalted at 5° Karka; Debilitated at 5° Makara; Moolatrikona in Dhanu (0°–10°).\n• Gemstone: Natural Yellow Sapphire (Pukhraj) set in pure gold.\n• Vedic Mantra: *Om Gram Greem Groum Sah Gurave Namaha*.\nBrihaspati is the divine preceptor. His drishti (aspect) is considered the most protective nectar in astrology, capable of neutralizing thousands of chart doshas. When prominent, Jupiter bestows righteous conduct, academic honors, healthy progeny, and financial abundance. Afflictions manifest as dogmatism, liver toxicity, metabolic obesity, and financial miscalculations.\n\n6. SHUKRA (VENUS) — Beauty, Diplomacy, and Creative Arts\n• Sanskrit Names: Daitya-Guru, Bhrigu, Kavi, Ushana\n• Nature: Supreme Natural Benefic (Rajas), Water element, Brahmin advisor\n• Governance: Romance, marriage partner, sensual luxury, vehicle conveyance, visual arts, music, kidneys, reproductive vitality (Shukra Dhatu).\n• Dignities: Exalted at 27° Meena; Debilitated at 27° Kanya; Moolatrikona in Tula (0°–15°).\n• Gemstone: Natural Diamond (Heera) or White Zircon in platinum or white gold.\n• Vedic Mantra: *Om Dram Dreem Droum Sah Shukraya Namaha*.\nShukra possesses Sanjeevani Vidya (the secret knowledge of spiritual revival). It teaches us to experience the divine through beauty, devotion, and refined human relationships. An afflicted Venus leads to marital infidelity, venereal imbalances, aesthetic vulgarity, and financial extravagance.\n\n7. SHANI (SATURN) — The Lord of Justice, Stoic Labor, and Time\n• Sanskrit Names: Sanaischara, Manda, Chhayaputra, Yama\n• Nature: Supreme Malefic (Tamas), Air element, Shudra servant\n• Governance: Longevity (Ayus), karma auditing, discipline, delay, poverty, chronic illness, structural engineering, mining, elder citizens, nervous system, teeth, joints.\n• Dignities: Exalted at 20° Tula; Debilitated at 20° Mesha; Moolatrikona in Kumbha (0°–20°).\n• Gemstone: Natural Blue Sapphire (Neelam) in iron or white gold (only after strict compatibility test!).\n• Vedic Mantra: *Om Pram Preem Proum Sah Shanaischaraya Namaha*.\nShani is the greatest spiritual teacher in the cosmos. Saturn does not punish; it purifies through time, delay, and detachment. Those who embrace humility, rigorous discipline, and selfless service find that Saturn rewards them with permanent status and unbreakable resilience.',

